{"seq":17,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:32:03.406Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"13b43f7dff514569f37aaad6dbe9ebecfd8e5bd27e78dba6faa6974d06144338","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, I've posted the list as a reply to your message in #coastal-team. I left out the Pellow Home Living / Covey & Lark items (PD-4821 and #8812).\n\nPellucid Harbor Logistics:\n- **#4419:** the Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length, and it's still open.\n- **#PD-8841:** chassis pool holds on double-booked gates (Gate 4B), from your Dec 2025 cutover recap. No status is given.\n- **No ticket number:** the Berth 2 yard map CSV import bug (your recap) and chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change (cheat sheet).\n\nDriftmoor Marine Freight:\n- **Feature request #882:** a bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by warehouse managers.\n- **#4419:** Moss's 2 Nov 2025 digest describes it as a barge slip 7 schedule sync ticket, with a patched manifest CSV requested before the 06:00 shift.\n- **No ticket number:** the Terminal B tide-table import macro failure, which engineering patched with a manual CSV.\n\nThe cheat sheet and the Nov 2025 digest give #4419 two different meanings, one for each account. I listed it under both and flagged it for you to check in the ticket system before the review.\n\nMost items have no status in the channels and notes I can see, so Kwame will need to confirm where each one stands."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000125"}}
